Package: flexloa
Type: Package
Title: Magnitude-Dependent Limits of Agreement via Variance-Stabilising
    Transformations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jeong-Hwa", "Yoon", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "yjh891114@snu.ac.kr"),
    person("Soon Ho", "Yoon", role = "aut"),
    person("Seokyung", "Hahn", role = "aut"))
Description: Conventional Bland-Altman limits of agreement (LOA) extended
    to measurement error that grows with the magnitude of the measurement.
    For each candidate variance-stabilising transformation (identity,
    square root, cube root, general n-th root, log) the package
    computes the conventional limits on the transformed scale,
    back-transforms them to curved LOA bands on the original scale,
    and reports the classical Bland-Altman diagnostics (normality of the
    transformed differences, the rank-correlation test of
    heteroscedasticity, the regression test of proportional bias, and
    empirical coverage) in a decision table, so that the transformation
    can be chosen on explicit grounds rather than by eye. General reader
    studies are converted to intra- and inter-reader difference pairs,
    and variance components for replicated multi-reader designs (intra-
    and inter-reader error) are estimated by REML or expected mean
    squares, following the modelling framework of Yoon, Yoon and Hahn
    (2019) <doi:10.1186/s12874-019-0727-7> and the transformation approach
    of Euser, Dekker and le Cessie (2008) <doi:10.1016/j.jclinepi.2007.11.003>.
